# C. Connections

## E-C01 Connection removed with open Pending order
- Behaviour: New orders blocked; open Pending order follows policy (auto-cancel or freeze for decision). Preferred safe default: block acceptance of new work; allow stockist to reject/cancel pending; do not allow new submits.
- Must not: Allow new orders on inactive connection.

## E-C02 Connection removed after Accepted but before dispatch
- Behaviour: Allow controlled completion or controlled cancel with reason; no new lines.
- Must not: Orphan fulfilment without status.

## E-C03 Connection removed after invoice issued
- Behaviour: Settlement and returns for historical docs remain processable.
- Must not: Delete invoices or block payment on valid dues solely due to disconnect.

## E-C04 Duplicate connection request while one Requested exists
- Behaviour: Block duplicate; show existing request.
- Must not: Create multiple Requested rows for same pair.

## E-C05 Pharmacy requests connection to itself / same business
- Behaviour: Impossible/blocked.
- Must not: Self-trade relationship.

## E-C06 Stockist approves then immediately disconnects
- Behaviour: Allowed; Active history retained; new trade blocked after disconnect.
- Must not: Erase approval audit.

## E-C07 Rejected pharmacy re-requests immediately
- Behaviour: Allowed unless cool-down/block policy.
- Must not: Auto-approve because previously connected.

## E-C08 Blocked pharmacy attempts browse pricing
- Behaviour: Deny private pricing/order.
- Must not: Leak customer-specific rates.

