# D. Catalogue, Cart & Ordering

## E-D01 Product deactivated while in cart
- Behaviour: Block place order for that line; require removal/update.
- Must not: Create order against inactive product.

## E-D02 Price changes after add-to-cart before submit
- Behaviour: Recheck at submit; show updated price confirmation or block if policy requires confirm.
- Must not: Silently charge unexpected price without snapshot clarity.

## E-D03 Stock becomes zero after accept
- Behaviour: Partial fulfilment path or cancel remainder; cannot pack unavailable qty.
- Must not: Negative inventory.

## E-D04 Empty order submit
- Behaviour: Block.
- Must not: Create empty Pending order.

## E-D05 Quantity zero / negative
- Behaviour: Validation fail.
- Must not: Persist invalid qty.

## E-D06 Duplicate product lines in cart
- Behaviour: Merge quantities.
- Must not: Ambiguous double lines unless intentionally separate batches later.

## E-D07 MOQ not met
- Behaviour: Block submit with reason.
- Must not: Accept under MOQ.

## E-D08 Max order qty exceeded
- Behaviour: Block.
- Must not: Accept above max.

## E-D09 Order while pharmacy suspended
- Behaviour: Block.
- Must not: Queue stealth orders.

## E-D10 Order while stockist suspended
- Behaviour: Block new submit/accept.
- Must not: Continue normal trade.

## E-D11 Reorder from historical discontinued product
- Behaviour: Allow add only if currently sellable; otherwise block line.
- Must not: Resurrect discontinued product into Active catalogue silently.

## E-D12 Notes contain “approved/paid” language
- Behaviour: Stored as note only; no status effect.
- Must not: Auto-transition states from notes.

