# E. Order Lifecycle Conflicts

## E-E01 Pharmacy cancels after Accepted
- Behaviour: Allowed only if rules say so; else deny.
- Must not: Cancel after dispatch without controlled process.

## E-E02 Stockist rejects after Accept
- Behaviour: Forbidden; use cancel-with-reason path if needed.
- Must not: Move Accepted → Rejected.

## E-E03 Double accept by two staff
- Behaviour: First wins; second sees Accepted.
- Must not: Duplicate side effects/reservations.

## E-E04 Cancel after invoice issued
- Behaviour: Do not silently cancel financial liability; require void/credit policy path.
- Must not: Delete invoice because order cancelled late.

## E-E05 Order closed while payment outstanding
- Behaviour: Closure rules must define whether operational close allowed with open dues; financial outstanding remains.
- Must not: Hide unpaid invoice because order closed.

## E-E06 Partial delivery forever unfinished
- Behaviour: Remainder cancel/complete policy + SLA reminders.
- Must not: Leave infinite Partially Delivered with no action path.

## E-E07 Edit lines after Packed
- Behaviour: Block.
- Must not: Mutate packed contents silently.

## E-E08 Accept order with all expired-only stock
- Behaviour: Block allocation/accept fulfilment; force reject/partial none.
- Must not: Dispatch expired medicines.

