# F. Inventory & Batches

## E-F01 Negative inventory attempt
- Behaviour: Block movement.
- Must not: Persist negative on hand.

## E-F02 Reserve more than available
- Behaviour: Block reservation.
- Must not: Over-reserve.

## E-F03 Batch expires after reservation before dispatch
- Behaviour: Block dispatch of that batch; reallocate or adjust order.
- Must not: Deliver expired reserved stock.

## E-F04 Batch recall after dispatch out for delivery
- Behaviour: Critical alert; stop completion if not delivered; initiate return/recovery process if delivered.
- Must not: Ignore recall.

## E-F05 Manual adjustment without reason
- Behaviour: Require reason.
- Must not: Silent stock edits.

## E-F06 Same batch number different products
- Behaviour: Allowed only if product-scoped uniqueness; prevent ambiguity in movements.
- Must not: Mix batch identity across products in one stock ledger incorrectly.

## E-F07 Quarantined stock allocated
- Behaviour: Block.
- Must not: Sell quarantined goods.

## E-F08 Pharmacy inventory not updated on receipt
- Behaviour: Receipt confirmation should create pharmacy stock movement when pharmacy inventory tracking enabled.
- Must not: Claim stock increased without receipt event.

## E-F09 Stock transfer creates disappearance
- Behaviour: Source decrease and destination increase in one controlled movement pair.
- Must not: One-sided transfer.

## E-F10 Near-expiry sold against FEFO preference
- Behaviour: Prefer earliest expiry sellable batch when auto-allocate; allow override with audit if permitted.
- Must not: Auto-pick expired.

