# G. Delivery Exceptions

## E-G01 Mark delivered without assignment
- Behaviour: Allow only if policy permits direct complete; else require valid delivery path.
- Must not: Skip creating delivery record when dispatch claimed.

## E-G02 Partial delivery quantities exceed packed
- Behaviour: Block.
- Must not: Deliver more than dispatched.

## E-G03 Pharmacy claims not received but stockist marks delivered
- Behaviour: Keep both signals; open dispute/support/shortage path; do not auto-delete delivery.
- Must not: Silent overwrite without audit.

## E-G04 Failed delivery then mark delivered without retry
- Behaviour: Require new successful attempt transition.
- Must not: Failed → Delivered direct.

## E-G05 Proof of delivery missing when mandatory
- Behaviour: Block complete or mark complete-with-exception per config.
- Must not: Ignore mandatory POD config.

## E-G06 Delivery to wrong address recorded
- Behaviour: Failed/wrong delivery reason; corrective redelivery; possible return to stockist.
- Must not: Force Paid/Closed automatically.

## E-G07 Multiple deliveries for one order
- Behaviour: Allowed for partial/multi-trip; quantities cumulative must not exceed ordered/packed rules.
- Must not: Double-count delivered qty.

