# I. Payments & Settlement

## E-I01 Duplicate payment submission (same reference)
- Behaviour: Flag/block or force On Hold review.
- Must not: Auto-approve duplicates.

## E-I02 Payment amount > total selected outstanding
- Behaviour: Block or allow unallocated remainder per advance-payment policy.
- Must not: Negative invoice outstanding.

## E-I03 Payment approved against already paid invoice
- Behaviour: Block allocation; leave unallocated or reject.
- Must not: Drive outstanding negative.

## E-I04 Concurrent approve payment and apply credit
- Behaviour: Serialise settlement; final outstanding = Grand Total − payments − credits ≥ 0.
- Must not: Race to negative.

## E-I05 Payment proof unreadable
- Behaviour: On Hold/Reject with reason.
- Must not: Approve without required proof when proof mandatory.

## E-I06 Pharmacy edits amount after submit
- Behaviour: Block; create new payment instead.
- Must not: Mutate under-review payment silently.

## E-I07 Stockist approves then tries reject
- Behaviour: Forbidden without controlled reversal process.
- Must not: Silent unapprove.

## E-I08 Payment for disconnected pair on old invoice
- Behaviour: Allowed for outstanding historical invoice.
- Must not: Block settlement of lawful dues solely due to disconnect.

## E-I09 Currency/method mismatch notes
- Behaviour: Hold/reject if method invalid.
- Must not: Convert inventively.

## E-I10 Split allocation doesn’t sum to payment
- Behaviour: Allow unallocated only if policy; else require full allocation.
- Must not: Lose money in allocation gaps without visibility.

