# J. Returns & Credit Notes

## E-J01 Return qty > delivered qty
- Behaviour: Block.
- Must not: Approve excess.

## E-J02 Return on undelivered items
- Behaviour: Block.
- Must not: Create return eligibility from Pending/Accepted only.

## E-J03 Return after eligibility window
- Behaviour: Block with reason.
- Must not: Accept late returns silently.

## E-J04 Credit exceeds approved return value
- Behaviour: Block.
- Must not: Over-credit.

## E-J05 Credit exceeds invoice outstanding on apply
- Behaviour: Apply min(remaining credit, outstanding); keep leftover credit.
- Must not: Negative outstanding.

## E-J06 Return approved but goods never received back when required
- Behaviour: Do not close until goods-back or policy waiver with audit.
- Must not: Restock inventory without receipt.

## E-J07 Restock damaged goods as sellable
- Behaviour: Disposition must quarantine/destroy if damaged; not Active sellable.
- Must not: Auto-restock damaged as sellable.

## E-J08 Credit note void after partial apply
- Behaviour: Only unapplied remainder voidable, or controlled reversal of applications first.
- Must not: Void away already applied credit without reversing settlement.

## E-J09 Duplicate return for same delivered units
- Behaviour: Track already returned qty; block exceed.
- Must not: Double credit same units.

## E-J10 Return while businesses suspended
- Behaviour: Generally allow processing historical returns; block new trade.
- Must not: Freeze dispute resolution forever without policy.

