# L. Support & Admin Governance

## E-L01 Support agent edits invoice totals
- Behaviour: Denied.
- Must not: Admin chat tools mutate finances.

## E-L02 Suspend business mid payment review
- Behaviour: Payment may still be decidable for historical dues per policy; new orders blocked.
- Must not: Auto-approve payments on suspension.

## E-L03 Ticket closed while investigation incomplete
- Behaviour: Allowed but reopen path exists; no automatic business mutation.
- Must not: Closing ticket void invoices.

## E-L04 Admin deactivates business with open receivables
- Behaviour: Retain all financial records; restrict login/trade; collections path defined.
- Must not: Wipe receivables.

---

# M. Analytics Conflicts

## E-M01 Dashboard total ≠ invoice list sum
- Behaviour: Trust invoice list/documents; mark analytics stale/recalculate.
- Must not: Change invoices to match chart.

## E-M02 Timezone period boundary differences
- Behaviour: Use consistent business timezone policy.
- Must not: Different dashboards using different day cutovers.

## E-M03 Export during recalculation
- Behaviour: Export consistent snapshot or delay with message.
- Must not: Half-old half-new mixed totals without notice.

---

# N. Concurrency & Double Submit

## E-N01 Double-click place order
- Behaviour: One order created; second attempt idempotent/blocked.
- Must not: Duplicate Pending orders.

## E-N02 Double-click approve payment
- Behaviour: One approval effect.
- Must not: Double allocation.

## E-N03 Accept and cancel racing
- Behaviour: Deterministic winner; loser gets state conflict error.
- Must not: Hybrid Accepted+Cancelled state.

## E-N04 Allocate same batch qty to two orders concurrently
- Behaviour: Reservations serialised; one fails if insufficient.
- Must not: Both succeed beyond available.

---

# O. Data Integrity & Deletion

## E-O01 Delete business with history
- Behaviour: Deactivate instead; retain history.
- Must not: Hard-delete financial graph.

## E-O02 Delete product with past order lines
- Behaviour: Discontinue/hide; keep master reference.
- Must not: Break historical order readability.

## E-O03 Delete notification deletes order
- Behaviour: Impossible; independent.
- Must not: Cascade into transactions.

## E-O04 User requests full data erase conflicting with statutory records
- Behaviour: Retain legally required business records; limit personal access fields per policy.
- Must not: Destroy invoices because user left.

---

# P. Business Merge / Structural Change (Current Handling)

## E-P01 Two pharmacies merge commercially
- Behaviour: Current product has no self-serve merge; admin/manual controlled process; do not auto-merge histories incorrectly.
- Must not: Casual combine of GST entities without governance.

## E-P02 Stockist adds second warehouse (not supported)
- Behaviour: Out of scope; single inventory model remains.
- Must not: Fake multi-warehouse via notes.

## E-P03 Inter-stockist transfer requested
- Behaviour: Out of scope currently; deny as product capability.
- Must not: Misuse returns/orders to simulate transfer without rules.

---

# Q. Pharmaceutical Safety Specific

## E-Q01 Expired medicine in pick list
- Behaviour: Block pick/dispatch.
- Must not: Complete delivery of expired sellable goods.

## E-Q02 Recalled batch already delivered
- Behaviour: Critical notifications; initiate return/recall response journey; credit paths as needed.
- Must not: Leave no operational trace.

## E-Q03 Schedule-sensitive products (if tracked)
- Behaviour: Enforce any configured eligibility constraints.
- Must not: Ignore configured restrictions.

## E-Q04 Temperature-sensitive note ignored
- Behaviour: Notes alone insufficient; if future cold-chain exists, separate controls; currently do not claim cold-chain compliance.
- Must not: Market unsupported compliance.

---

# R. Partial Success Patterns

## E-R01 Catalogue import 900/1000 rows valid
- Behaviour: Import valid rows; report invalid rows; no silent all-or-nothing confusion—policy must be explicit (prefer partial with report).
- Must not: Mark full success when rows failed.

## E-R02 Multi-invoice payment where one invoice becomes paid concurrently
- Behaviour: Allocate to still-open invoices; leftover unallocated/adjust; show clear result.
- Must not: Fail entire payment after money intent without clear state.

## E-R03 Network drop after order created
- Behaviour: On retry, do not create second order if first succeeded; show existing order.
- Must not: Duplicate on retry.

---

# S. Large-Volume / Practical Limits

## E-S01 Order with extremely large line count
- Behaviour: Enforce practical max lines; block beyond.
- Must not: Hang user journey without feedback.

## E-S02 Export million rows
- Behaviour: Require narrower filters / async export.
- Must not: Fail silently.

## E-S03 Search with only 1 character
- Behaviour: Require minimum characters or show guided results.
- Must not: Unbounded heavy scans without constraint.

